    "paid_argument": "Actual last D vs B_i gives d≥x. With a>0 let L=x/2+a. After the last C_i deviates to A_i, first responder can guarantee L using an old A_j: every last BR avoids C_j/A_j/B_j, by comparison to D or another old A_l. k≥3 supplies that other group. Both true responders avoid A_i/C_i because each has an untouched-old-group A_l menu of value L; they cannot both choose B_i because last D strictly improves x/3+b/2 to d+b/2. Thus deviator keeps all a_i and at least x/2, so root-node IC x≥x/2+a gives a≤x/2. D is disjoint from X_i. a=0 is immediate and the strict comparisons persist at b=0. All A_i plus D cover every client, giving exact OPT and OPT/W≤3/2.",
